00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:26.420
you have that era, right?

00:28:26.420 --> 00:28:27.253
- [Jocelyne] The Undertaker.

00:28:27.253 --> 00:28:30.920
- That to me is fascinating
about sports in America.

00:28:30.920 --> 00:28:33.520
- Well, if you think of hockey,
not just women's hockey,

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:36.520
but I think hockey's the
last professional sport

00:28:36.520 --> 00:28:41.140
where it's a team, don't bring
any attention to yourself,

00:28:41.140 --> 00:28:44.380
don't have any personality and
I feel hockey's kind of like

00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:48.287
the last sport that's finally
kind of being accepting

00:28:48.287 --> 00:28:51.500
of that because I mean,
you look at P.K. Subban

00:28:51.500 --> 00:28:55.180
and the amount of negative attention

00:28:55.180 --> 00:28:57.310
he gets for, well he's off on his own,

00:28:57.310 --> 00:29:00.310
he's doing his own, people are
allowed to have personality.

00:29:00.310 --> 00:29:04.260
- The NHL was one of VaynerMedia's
first clients in 2009

00:29:04.260 --> 00:29:07.410
and I remember Brendan
Shanahan had me come and speak

00:29:07.410 --> 00:29:09.710
to all the kids that
were about to get drafted

00:29:09.710 --> 00:29:12.300
and I was spitting all
this thoughts about what

00:29:12.300 --> 00:29:15.530
social media can do and all
the stuff that is now accepted

00:29:15.530 --> 00:29:18.883
and to your point, and it's
the same thing in baseball,

00:29:20.060 --> 00:29:22.580
and it's the same thing
for rookies in any sport.

00:29:22.580 --> 00:29:23.557
Right?

00:29:23.557 --> 00:29:28.557
Us normal people don't
understand the judgment pressures

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:32.710
inside of a locker room
that, go do anything,

00:29:32.710 --> 00:29:37.240
that isn't on team and
the NBA is the one place

00:29:37.240 --> 00:29:39.940
where that is embraced and
that is the biggest reason

00:29:39.940 --> 00:29:43.180
it is exploded in the direction it has,

00:29:43.180 --> 00:29:45.470
because there is individualism.

00:29:45.470 --> 00:29:48.070
That is accepted while
being able to in-parallel,

00:29:48.070 --> 00:29:50.000
hold form, 100%.

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:53.346
- On top of having individualism
and not it being judged,

00:29:53.346 --> 00:29:56.453
but then being able to
promote it within the team.

00:29:57.290 --> 00:29:58.970
- And letting merit play out, right?

00:29:58.970 --> 00:30:01.520
Individualism in basketball
is really fascinating.

